      "id": 1,
      "text": "The Ojibwe called the river Akiko‑zibi, meaning 'Kettle River,' a nod to the deep glacial kettles that shaped the landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/kettle_river_minnesota",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Finnish settlers established the community of Finland north of the Soo Line railroad, while Polish immigrants founded the original Kettle River settlement to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/kettle_river_minnesota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1918 Cloquet fire, ignited by sparks from passing locomotives, scorched the town and left only a brick bank standing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kettle_River%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every August, Kettle River celebrates Ma and Pa Kettle Days with a pancake breakfast, parade, pageant, mud bog, and street dances.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kettle_River%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Glacial faults and activity create a dynamic runoff‑driven river system, with low water levels in late summer limiting accessibility.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/kettle_river_minnesota",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
